---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
---

<CaseStudy
  name="Hank"
  tagline="is a social network focused on fighting social isolation amongst older adults."
  shareImage="hank-app-screenshot"
>
  <Fragment slot="meta">
    <p><strong>Years</strong> 2020-2024</p>
    <p><strong>Role</strong> Co-founder, Head of Product &amp; Design</p>
    <p><strong>Responsibilities</strong> Product Design, User Research, Many other hats</p>
    <p><strong>Collaborators</strong> 1 product manager, 4 engineers</p>
    <p><strong>Platforms</strong> iOS, Web</p>
    <p class="callout">Hank was acquired by Wider Circle in 2024.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      I co-founded Hank with Brian Park in 2020 in the midst of the Covid-19 pandemic. We built a social platform
      designed for older adults to find and organize in-person activities, build friendships, and live healthy and
      socially rich lives.
    </p>
    <p>
      I was responsible for every single touchpoint for Hank including the product, brand (with assistance from an
      agency), email, product copy, social media creative, customer service, and more.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots', alt: 'Hank main product views' }]} lead="Main product views." eager>
    Hank connects members to each other via in-person activities and helps them built relationships via chat features.
  </Figure>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots-UI-snippets-1', alt: 'Hank UI snippets' }]} tight />
    <Figure
      images={[
        { name: 'hank-printed-card', alt: 'Hank printed card' },
        { name: 'member-pins', alt: 'Hank member pins' },
      ]}
      lead="Assorted UI and brand snippets."
    >
      I was responsible for any piece of software and brand touched by a end and internal users.
    </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Fighting social isolation amongst older adults.</h2>
    <p>
      Our members were typically adults 55+ who had undergone some sort of precipitating event that highlighted their
      loneliness - moving away from friends to be closer to grandchildren, losing a partner, or retiring and falling out
      of touch with coworkers. We sought to build a playful social experience with an emphasis on in-person
      relationships.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots-activities2', alt: 'Hank activities list, detail, and creation form' }]}
    lead="Cool things to do and people to do them with."
  >
    Hank is focused around meeting up with other members in-person and building human connections in the real world.
  </Figure>

  <figure class="video">
    <video src="/media/Activity-form-demo-16x9-1.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"
      aria-label="Demo of the Hank activity creation form"></video>
    <figcaption>
      <strong>Activity creation form.</strong>
      <span class="muted">We went through multiple rounds of usability testing and iterations to make the form simple to use.</span>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <Figure
    images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots-profile', alt: 'Hank member profile screens' }]}
    lead="Making an online community feel more human."
  >
    We have invested in content-rich user profiles and delightful interaction touches to make the product feel warmer
    and more welcoming.
  </Figure>

  <Figure
    images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots-messages', alt: 'Hank group chat on desktop and iOS' }]}
    lead="Keeping members connected."
  >
    Members that join an activity are automatically added to a full-featured group chat (powered by Stream) that allows
    members to connect with one another.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Using AI to help scale activity supply</h2>
    <p>
      As Hank grows, it is crucial that we maintain a sufficient volume of activities in each market. We have been
      experimenting with using generative AI to find local activities and create brand new ones. Hank team members can
      then manually screen activities before editing, deleting, or publishing.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots-babyface', alt: 'Dashboard listing AI-generated activity drafts' }]}
    lead="Dashboard for AI-generated drafts."
  >
    Drafts can be generated, edited, and published from this dashboard. In the background, AI-powered scripting tools
    generate activities drawn from different sources and processed to help ensure that data is not being hallucinated.
  </Figure>

  <Figure
    images={[{ name: 'hank-screenshots-ai-draft', alt: 'Editing an AI-generated activity draft beside its source' }]}
    lead="Editing AI-generated drafts."
  >
    Drafts always refers back to the source material to double-check content and decrease risk of hallucinations. The
    UI also communicates wherever there were issues parsing data to be fed into Hank's activity schema.
  </Figure>
</CaseStudy>

<style>
  .video {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(60px, 8vw, 100px);
  }
  .video video {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  .video figcaption {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
</style>
